const STASHES={
love:{n:"Love",d:"Romance, tenderness and keeping love alive",c:"#f4a6b8"},
confidence:{n:"Confidence",d:"Speak up, stand tall, be heard",c:"#f2c46d"},
mind:{n:"Sharp Mind",d:"Think clearly, learn fast, grow wise",c:"#9fd3e6"},
enterprise:{n:"Enterprise",d:"Ideas to earn, save and build",c:"#a7d99a"},
smile:{n:"Smile",d:"Laughter, lightness and joy",c:"#ffb38a"},
world:{n:"Love Around the World",d:"Romance from China, India, Turkey, Arabia, Korea and Japan",c:"#c9b6ff"},
his:{n:"His Heart",d:"What a husband needs, gently explained",c:"#86d0c4"},
hers:{n:"Her Heart",d:"For husbands: how to love her well",c:"#e7a3ff"}};
/* which stashes make up each person’s daily deck */
const DECK={w:["love","his","world","confidence","mind","enterprise","smile"],h:["hers","love","world","mind","enterprise","smile"]};

/* each card: s stash, t title, b body, q quote [text, by], f faith [text, source], a try-it */
const CARDS=[
/* LOVE */
{s:"love",t:"Count the ways",q:["How do I love thee? Let me count the ways.","Elizabeth Barrett Browning, 1850"],b:"Love grows when we say it out loud. You don’t need big words. Small, clear words are enough.",f:["The Prophet ﷺ said: if you love someone, tell them.","Abu Dawud 5124"],a:"Send him one reason you love him today. Just one line."},
{s:"love",t:"The same side of the cup",b:"Aisha would drink from a cup and pass it to the Prophet ﷺ. He looked for the place her lips had touched, and drank from that very spot. The best of people noticed the smallest things.",f:["Narrated by Aisha (ra).","Muslim 300"],a:"Notice one small thing about him today, and tell him you noticed."},
{s:"love",t:"Race me",b:"On a journey, the Prophet ﷺ said to Aisha, “Come, let’s race.” She won. Years later they raced again and he won. He laughed and said, “This one is for that one.” Play keeps love young.",f:["Narrated by Aisha (ra).","Abu Dawud 2578"],a:"Do something playful today. Send him a silly photo or a funny voice note."},
{s:"love",t:"Blessed with her love",b:"Years after Khadijah died, the Prophet ﷺ still spoke about her with love. He said, “I was blessed with her love.” He even sent gifts to her friends. Real love does not fade with time.",f:["Muslim 2435; Bukhari 3818",""],a:"Tell him one memory from your early days together that you still treasure."},
{s:"love",t:"Spaces in your togetherness",q:["Let there be spaces in your togetherness.","Kahlil Gibran, The Prophet, 1923"],b:"Being apart is hard. But distance can also grow love, if you fill it with care. Missing someone shows the heart is alive.",f:["When you pray for someone who is away, an angel says: “And for you the same.”","Muslim 2733"],a:"Make dua for him by name tonight. Then tell him you did."},
{s:"love",t:"Love that does not change",q:["Love is not love which alters when it alteration finds.","Shakespeare, Sonnet 116"],b:"Life changes. Children come, work gets busy, homes move. True love stays steady through all of it.",f:["Allah placed between spouses “affection and mercy.” Affection is the warm feeling. Mercy is what holds you when feelings are tired.","Qur’an 30:21"],a:"Think of one hard season you two came through. Thank Allah for it."},
{s:"love",t:"The best is yet to be",q:["Grow old along with me! The best is yet to be.","Robert Browning, 1864"],b:"Many couples say the sweetest years came later, after the hard ones. Love is a long road. Enjoy each part of it.",f:["“Our Lord, give us joy in our spouses and children, and make us leaders of the righteous.”","Qur’an 25:74"],a:"Say this dua today for both of you."},
{s:"love",t:"The tiny moments",b:"A researcher, Dr John Gottman, watched couples for years. Happy couples answered each other’s small moments, like “Look at that!” or a quick message, most of the time. Couples who broke up mostly ignored them.",f:["“The best of you are the best to their families.”","Tirmidhi 3895"],a:"Reply to his next small message warmly, even if you are busy."},
{s:"love",t:"Five sweet for one sour",b:"In Gottman’s research, happy couples had about five good moments for every bad one, even during an argument. A kind word, a laugh or a soft touch balances a hard word.",f:["“A good word is charity.”","Bukhari 2989"],a:"After any small argument, add five sweet things. Count them."},
{s:"love",t:"How does he feel loved?",b:"Gary Chapman found that people feel love in five main ways: kind words, time together, gifts, help with tasks, and touch. Most people have one favourite. Learn his.",f:["“Give gifts and you will love one another.”","al-Adab al-Mufrad 594"],a:"Ask him in the chat: which of the five makes you feel most loved?"},
{s:"love",t:"Sweet names",b:"The Prophet ﷺ had a pet name for Aisha. He called her “Aish”. One day he said, “O Aish, this is Jibril, and he sends you salam.” Sweet names are Sunnah.",f:["Bukhari 3217",""],a:"Give him a sweet name only you use. Try it in the chat today."},
{s:"love",t:"He listened to her story",b:"Aisha once told the Prophet ﷺ a long story about eleven women and their husbands. He listened to all of it. Then he said, “I am to you as Abu Zar‘ was to Umm Zar‘,” the best husband in the story.",f:["Bukhari 5189",""],a:"Tell him a story today. Let him listen. Then listen to his."},
{s:"love",t:"Two souls, one kind",q:["Whatever our souls are made of, his and mine are the same.","Emily Brontë, Wuthering Heights, 1847"],b:"The deepest romance is feeling truly known. Not just loved, but understood.",f:["“Souls are like gathered troops. Those who know each other come close.”","Bukhari 3336"],a:"Tell him one thing about you that he might not know yet."},
{s:"love",t:"If ever two were one",q:["If ever two were one, then surely we.","Anne Bradstreet, 1678"],b:"Marriage makes two people a team. You cover each other’s weak spots and celebrate each other’s wins.",f:["“They are a garment for you, and you are a garment for them.”","Qur’an 2:187"],a:"Ask him: what is one way I can support you this week?"},
{s:"love",t:"Look the same way",b:"The writer Antoine de Saint-Exupéry said love is not only looking at each other. It is looking together in the same direction. Shared dreams make love strong.",f:["“Allah makes a way for those who fear Him.”","Qur’an 65:2"],a:"Share one dream for your family in five years. Ask for his."},
{s:"love",t:"The happiest feeling",q:["The supreme happiness of life is the conviction that we are loved.","Victor Hugo, Les Misérables, 1862"],b:"Everyone wants to feel loved. When you show him love, you give him the greatest gift in life.",f:["Allah says: when My servant comes close to Me, I love him.","Bukhari 6502"],a:"Make sure he goes to sleep today knowing he is loved."},
{s:"love",t:"Zaynab’s necklace",b:"When Zaynab’s husband was taken captive, she sent her most precious necklace to free him. It was a wedding gift from her mother, Khadijah. When the Prophet ﷺ saw it, his heart melted, and her husband was set free.",f:["Abu Dawud 2692",""],a:"What would you give for him? Tell him in a postcard."},
{s:"love",t:"The wise welcome",b:"Umm Sulaym had sad news for her husband. She waited. First she welcomed him, fed him and let him rest. Then she shared the news gently. Good timing is a kind of love.",f:["The Prophet ﷺ prayed for them, and Allah blessed them with a son.","Bukhari 5470"],a:"Before you share a problem with him, ask: “Is now a good time?”"},
{s:"love",t:"Start with a smile",b:"The first minute of a call sets the mood for the whole call. Start with a smile and a sweet word, not a problem. Problems can come after love.",f:["“Your smile for your brother is charity.”","Tirmidhi 1956"],a:"Start his next call with: “I’m so happy to hear your voice.”"},
{s:"love",t:"A little mystery",b:"Therapist Esther Perel teaches that longing needs a little space and surprise. Couples who live apart can use this. Plan small surprises. Keep a little mystery.",f:["“Allah is beautiful and loves beauty.”","Muslim 91"],a:"Plan one small surprise for his next visit. Don’t tell him!"},
{s:"love",t:"Say thank you",b:"Research by Dr Sara Algoe shows that saying “thank you” to your partner makes both of you feel closer. Gratitude is like water for love.",f:["“Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah.”","Abu Dawud 4811"],a:"Thank him today for one thing he does that people don’t see."},
{s:"love",t:"Half agony, half hope",q:["You pierce my soul. I am half agony, half hope.","Jane Austen, Persuasion, 1817"],b:"In this story, a shy man could not say his feelings, so he wrote a letter. Letters can say what our mouths are too shy to say.",f:["Allah taught by the pen.","Qur’an 96:4"],a:"Write him a postcard in Sakinah today."},
/* CONFIDENCE */
{s:"confidence",t:"She spoke, and Allah heard",b:"Khawlah had a problem with her husband. She went to the Prophet ﷺ and argued her case. Allah sent a whole surah about her: “Allah has heard the words of the woman who argued with you.”",f:["Qur’an 58:1",""],a:"Share your opinion once today, calmly and clearly."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Her advice saved the day",b:"At Hudaybiyyah, the Companions were upset and did not move. Umm Salamah calmly advised the Prophet ﷺ: go out, do the act yourself, and they will follow. He did, and they followed.",f:["Bukhari 2731",""],a:"When you have a good idea, say it. Calm words carry weight."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Ask for what you need",b:"The women of Madinah told the Prophet ﷺ: “The men take all your time. Give us a day.” He gave them their own day to learn. Asking clearly is not rude. It is wise.",f:["Bukhari 101",""],a:"Ask for one thing you need this week, clearly and kindly."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Names are music",b:"Dale Carnegie, a famous teacher of people skills, said a person’s name is the sweetest sound to them. Using names makes people feel seen.",f:["The Prophet ﷺ called people by the names they loved.",""],a:"Greet three people today using their names."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Never run out of words",b:"Not sure what to say? Use FORD: Family, Occupation, Recreation, Dreams. Ask about their family, their work, what they enjoy, and what they hope for.",f:["“Spread salam among you.”","Muslim 54"],a:"Use FORD in your next chat with a friend or neighbour."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Ask, then ask again",b:"A Harvard study found that people who ask follow-up questions are liked more. A follow-up question says: I really heard you.",f:["The Prophet ﷺ would turn his whole body to face the person speaking to him.","Shama’il al-Tirmidhi"],a:"In your next talk, ask one follow-up question: “And then what happened?”"},
{s:"confidence",t:"Breathe before you speak",b:"Nervous? Take a slow breath in. Then breathe out even slower. A long breath out tells your body to calm down. Then speak.",f:["“Verily, in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find rest.”","Qur’an 13:28"],a:"Before your next important talk, take three slow breaths and say “Bismillah.”"},
{s:"confidence",t:"The power of a pause",b:"You don’t have to answer fast. A short pause before you answer makes you look calm and wise, and gives you time to choose good words.",f:["“Speak good, or stay silent.”","Bukhari 6018"],a:"Today, pause for two seconds before you answer a question."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Your worth is not online",b:"Social media shows other people’s best moments. Comparing your normal day to their best day steals your joy.",f:["“Look at those below you in worldly things, not above you. That way you will not belittle Allah’s blessings.”","Muslim 2963"],a:"Write three blessings you have that someone else is praying for."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Your first sentence",b:"Before you say a word, your face speaks. A warm smile tells people you are kind and confident. It opens doors.",f:["“I never saw anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”","Tirmidhi 3641"],a:"Smile first at everyone you meet today."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Strong enough to say “I don’t know”",b:"Imam Malik, one of the greatest scholars, was asked many questions. For many of them he simply said, “I don’t know.” Confident people are not afraid to say it.",f:["“Above every person of knowledge is one more knowing.”","Qur’an 12:76"],a:"If you don’t know something today, say so. Then go and find out."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Skill brings confidence",b:"Rufaida al-Aslamiyyah set up a tent to care for the wounded in the Prophet’s ﷺ time. She is remembered as one of the first nurses in Islam. When you are good at something, confidence follows.",f:["“Allah loves, when one of you does a job, that he does it well.”","al-Bayhaqi, Shu‘ab al-Iman"],a:"Pick one skill you want to be known for. Practise it for 15 minutes."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Dress for your own heart",b:"Looking nice is not only for others. When you dress well, even at home, you feel brighter and walk taller.",f:["“Allah is beautiful and loves beauty.”","Muslim 91"],a:"Wear something today that makes you feel lovely. Send him a photo if you like."},
{s:"confidence",t:"One new word a day",b:"People who have more words find it easier to express themselves. Learn one new English word each day and use it once.",f:["Allah taught Adam the names of all things.","Qur’an 2:31"],a:"Today’s word: “grateful”. Use it in a sentence to him."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Tell it as a story",b:"People remember stories more than facts. A good story has three parts: what happened, what went wrong, and how it ended.",f:["Allah says the Qur’an tells “the best of stories.”","Qur’an 12:3"],a:"Tell him about your day as a short story with those three parts."},
{s:"confidence",t:"Say no kindly",b:"You can say no without being rude. Try: “Thank you for thinking of me, but I can’t this time.” Clear and kind.",f:["“The strong one is the one who controls himself when angry.”","Bukhari 6114"],a:"Practise one kind “no” today, even a small one."},
{s:"confidence",t:"More than one story",b:"Nigerian writer Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie warns about “the danger of a single story”. You are not only one label. You are a wife, a mother, a thinker, a friend, and much more.",f:["“Allah does not look at your faces or your wealth, but at your hearts and your deeds.”","Muslim 2564"],a:"Write five words that describe who you are, beyond “housewife”."},
/* MIND */
{s:"mind",t:"The first word: Read",b:"The very first word Allah revealed was “Read”. Reading feeds the mind like food feeds the body.",f:["“Read, in the name of your Lord who created.”","Qur’an 96:1"],a:"Read ten pages of a good book today."},
{s:"mind",t:"Ten minutes a day",b:"Ten minutes of reading a day can finish about a book a month. That is twelve books a year, from just ten minutes.",f:["“The most beloved deeds to Allah are the consistent ones, even if small.”","Bukhari 6464"],a:"Choose your ten minutes today. Set a timer."},
{s:"mind",t:"Ask why five times",b:"When a problem keeps coming back, ask “Why?” five times. Each answer takes you deeper, until you find the real cause.",f:["“Ask the people of knowledge if you do not know.”","Qur’an 16:43"],a:"Pick one small problem at home. Ask “why” five times."},
{s:"mind",t:"Write it out",b:"Psychologist James Pennebaker found that writing about your feelings for a few minutes can lift stress. Paper holds what the heart can’t.",f:["“Verily, with hardship comes ease.”","Qur’an 94:6"],a:"Write for five minutes tonight about how you feel. No one needs to read it."},
{s:"mind",t:"Sleep is smart",b:"Sleep helps the brain save what you learned and clear out what you don’t need. Tired minds make poor choices.",f:["“We made your sleep for rest.”","Qur’an 78:9"],a:"Go to bed 30 minutes earlier tonight."},
{s:"mind",t:"Think, ask, then trust",b:"Good decisions have three steps. Think it through. Ask people you trust. Then pray istikhara and trust Allah.",f:["“Consult them in the matter. Then, when you decide, rely on Allah.”","Qur’an 3:159"],a:"Have a decision coming? Ask him for his view today."},
{s:"mind",t:"Curious like Aisha",b:"Aisha (ra) never heard something she did not understand without asking about it. Her questions made her one of the greatest teachers of Islam.",f:["Bukhari 103",""],a:"Ask one “why” or “how” question today about anything you are curious about."},
{s:"mind",t:"Teach to learn",b:"The best way to learn something is to teach it. If you can explain it simply, you truly understand it.",f:["“Convey from me, even one verse.”","Bukhari 3461"],a:"Teach the children one thing you learned this week."},
{s:"mind",t:"Walk and think",b:"A Stanford study found people came up with more creative ideas while walking than sitting. Stuck? Take a short walk.",f:["Allah tells us to travel the earth and reflect.","Qur’an 29:20"],a:"Take a ten-minute walk today without your phone."},
{s:"mind",t:"Check before you share",b:"WhatsApp is full of rumours. A smart mind checks before sharing. Ask: who said this? Is it true? Does it help?",f:["“If a news-bearer comes to you with news, verify it.”","Qur’an 49:6"],a:"Before forwarding anything today, check if it is true."},
{s:"mind",t:"The memory palace",b:"To remember a list, picture each item in a room of your home: eggs at the door, rice on the sofa. Then walk through the house in your mind.",f:["“My Lord, increase me in knowledge.”","Qur’an 20:114"],a:"Use the memory palace for your next shopping list."},
{s:"mind",t:"Let yourself be bored",b:"Great ideas often come when the mind is quiet. If we fill every second with the phone, ideas have no room to grow.",f:["Allah praises those who reflect on the creation of the heavens and earth.","Qur’an 3:191"],a:"Put your phone away for 30 minutes today. Notice your thoughts."},
{s:"mind",t:"20 hours to learn",b:"Writer Josh Kaufman says about 20 hours of focused practice can make you good enough at most new skills. That is 30 minutes a day for six weeks.",f:["“Seeking knowledge is a duty on every Muslim.”","Ibn Majah 224"],a:"Pick one skill. Write down your first 30 minutes of practice."},
{s:"mind",t:"Knowledge that helps",b:"Imam al-Shafi‘i said: knowledge is not what you memorise, it is what benefits you. Learn things you will use.",f:["“O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit.”","Muslim 2722"],a:"Use one thing you learned this week, today."},
/* ENTERPRISE */
{s:"enterprise",t:"Khadijah, the businesswoman",b:"Khadijah ran trade caravans in Makkah. She hired Muhammad ﷺ because he was honest, and she trusted him with her goods. Honesty is a business’s best money.",f:["When revelation first came, she comforted him and stood by him.","Bukhari 3"],a:"Write down one thing you are good at that people might pay for."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"The longest hand",b:"The Prophet ﷺ said the wife with “the longest hand” would join him first. It was Zaynab bint Jahsh. She worked with her hands, earned money, and gave it in charity.",f:["Muslim 2452",""],a:"Think of one handmade thing you could sell."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"Start from your kitchen",b:"Many big businesses started small. Small chops, zobo, cakes, kunun aya, spices. Start by selling to ten people you already know.",f:["“No one eats better food than what he earns with his own hands.”","Bukhari 2072"],a:"List ten people who might buy something from you."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"Sell what people ask for",b:"What do friends always ask you for help with? Braiding, cooking, sewing, advice? That is a clue to a business.",f:["Allah made people different so they need one another’s skills.","Qur’an 43:32"],a:"Ask two friends: “What do you think I’m good at?”"},
{s:"enterprise",t:"WhatsApp is your shop",b:"Use your WhatsApp status like a shop window. Take photos in daylight. Show the price. Post a little every day.",f:["“Allah has made trade lawful.”","Qur’an 2:275"],a:"Take three nice daylight photos of something you make."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"Price with courage",b:"Price = cost of materials + your time + profit. Don’t work for free. Your time has value.",f:["“Give the worker his wage before his sweat dries.”","Ibn Majah 2443"],a:"Work out the real cost of one thing you make."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"Keep a money book",b:"Write down every naira that comes in and goes out. In one month you will see where your money really goes.",f:["“When you take a debt for a fixed time, write it down.”","Qur’an 2:282"],a:"Start a money book today: date, item, amount."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"The honest seller",b:"Customers return to sellers they trust. Never hide a fault. Never give less than you promise.",f:["“The honest, trustworthy trader will be with the prophets, the truthful and the martyrs.”","Tirmidhi 1209"],a:"Think of one way to show honesty to a customer."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"One skill, many incomes",b:"If you can sew, you can make clothes, fix clothes, teach sewing, and sell patterns. One skill can open many doors.",f:["“Allah loves, when one of you does a job, that he does it well.”","al-Bayhaqi"],a:"Write three ways to earn from one skill you have."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"Small and steady wins",b:"A business that grows a little every week beats one that starts big and stops. Steady effort wins.",f:["“The most beloved deeds to Allah are the consistent ones, even if small.”","Bukhari 6464"],a:"Choose one small business step to do every day this week."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"She began with fashion",b:"Folorunso Alakija, one of Nigeria’s richest women, started out in fashion with her own clothing label before she went into oil. Big journeys start with one step.",f:["“Allah does not change a people until they change what is in themselves.”","Qur’an 13:11"],a:"Write down your “one step” for this month."},
{s:"enterprise",t:"Learn for free",b:"You can learn baking, sewing, design or bookkeeping on YouTube for free. A phone can be a school.",f:["“Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge, Allah makes easy a path to Paradise.”","Muslim 2699"],a:"Watch one 10-minute tutorial on a skill you want."},
/* LOVE AROUND THE WORLD */
{s:"world",t:"Holding your hand",img:"tulips",from:"China",q:["Holding your hand, I will grow old with you.","The Book of Songs, China, about 2,600 years ago"],b:"This line is one of the oldest love promises in the world. Chinese couples still say it today. It is not about one big day. It is about walking side by side for a whole life.",f:["“Our Lord, give us joy in our spouses and children.”","Qur’an 25:74"],a:"Tell him one thing you want you two to do when you are old."},
{s:"world",t:"The bridge of birds",img:"moon2",from:"China",b:"An old Chinese story tells of a weaver girl and a cowherd who loved each other but were kept apart by a river of stars. Once a year, birds fly together to make a bridge so they can meet. The poet Qin Guan wrote: if two hearts are united forever, why must they be together every day and night?",f:["When you pray for someone far away, an angel says: “And for you the same.”","Muslim 2733"],a:"Tell him: “Our hearts are together, even when we are apart.”"},
{s:"world",t:"One moon, two places",img:"moon",from:"China",q:["Though a thousand miles apart, we share the same beautiful moon.","Su Shi, China, 1076"],b:"Su Shi wrote this on a moonlit night, missing his brother far away. Today, Chinese families and couples who live apart send this line to each other. Wherever you are, you look at the same moon.",f:["Allah made the sun a light and the moon a glow.","Qur’an 10:5"],a:"Tonight, look at the moon. Send him a message: “I’m looking at our moon.”"},
{s:"world",t:"Hearts that understand",img:"peony",from:"China",b:"The Tang poet Li Shangyin wrote that two loving hearts are joined by a fine thread, so they understand each other without words. A look, a smile, a pause: love learns to read them.",f:["“He brought their hearts together.”","Qur’an 8:63"],a:"Guess what he needs today, and give it before he asks."},
{s:"world",t:"A palace for love",img:"taj",from:"India",b:"The Taj Mahal in India was built by the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan in memory of his beloved wife, Mumtaz Mahal. She travelled with him everywhere, even on long journeys. Millions visit every year to see what love can build.",f:["“Among His signs: He created for you spouses that you may find peace in them.”","Qur’an 30:21"],a:"If your love could build something, what would it be? Tell him."},
{s:"world",t:"Numberless times",img:"henna2",from:"India",q:["I seem to have loved you in numberless forms, numberless times.","Rabindranath Tagore, Unending Love"],b:"Tagore, the Indian poet who won the Nobel Prize in 1913, wrote about a love that feels older than time. When love is deep, it feels like you have always known each other.",f:["“Souls are like gathered troops. Those who know each other come close.”","Bukhari 3336"],a:"Tell him: “I feel like I’ve always known you.”"},
{s:"world",t:"Letters that talk",img:"paper",from:"India",b:"The great Urdu poet Mirza Ghalib was famous for his letters. He wrote them so warmly that friends said reading them felt like sitting and talking with him. A good letter makes distance smaller.",f:["Allah taught by the pen.","Qur’an 96:4"],a:"Write him a short letter in your own words. Send it as a postcard."},
{s:"world",t:"The sultan who wrote poems",img:"rose1",from:"Turkey",b:"Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent ruled a great empire. When he was away on long journeys, he wrote love poems to his wife Hürrem under the pen name Muhibbi, which means “the lover”. He called her his moonlight and his closest friend. She wrote letters back.",f:["“A good word is charity.”","Bukhari 2989"],a:"Give him three sweet names in your next message, like the sultan did."},
{s:"world",t:"Love for Allah’s sake",img:"pinkroses",from:"Turkey",b:"The Turkish poet Yunus Emre is remembered for the idea: we love the created because of the Creator. When love is for Allah, it grows purer and lasts longer.",f:["Allah will say: “Where are those who loved each other for My sake? Today I shade them in My shade.”","Muslim 2566"],a:"Tell him: “I love you for the sake of Allah.”"},
{s:"world",t:"Never really apart",img:"sakura",from:"Turkey",b:"Rumi, the great poet who lived and died in Konya, Turkey, taught that true lovers do not finally meet one day. They were inside each other’s hearts all along.",f:["“He created you from a single soul, and from it He created its mate.”","Qur’an 4:1"],a:"Tell him one way he lives in your heart every day."},
{s:"world",t:"The ring of the dove",img:"rings",from:"Arabia & Andalus",b:"Ibn Hazm was a great Muslim scholar of law in Islamic Spain. In 1022 he also wrote a whole book about love, “The Ring of the Dove.” He listed its signs: you want to keep looking at the one you love, you hurry to where they are, and your heart beats fast when they arrive.",f:["Love is part of being human. Islam gives it a home.",""],a:"Tell him the first moment you knew you loved him."},
{s:"world",t:"The garden of lovers",img:"arch",from:"Arabia",b:"Imam Ibn al-Qayyim wrote a book about love called “The Garden of Lovers.” He praised love that leads to marriage and stays inside what pleases Allah. The best love lets you love Allah more, not less.",f:["“We have not seen anything better for two who love each other than marriage.”","Ibn Majah 1847"],a:"Thank Allah today, out loud, for your marriage."},
{s:"world",t:"Layla and Majnun",img:"moon2",from:"Arabia",b:"Qays loved Layla so much that people called him Majnun, “the one gone mad.” The story is beautiful but sad. Love without balance and without marriage brings pain. Islam gives love a safe home, so it can grow without breaking you.",f:["“We have not seen anything better for two who love each other than marriage.”","Ibn Majah 1847"],a:"Thank Allah that your love has a home."},
{s:"world",t:"Love gives itself",img:"bouquet",from:"Lebanon",q:["Love gives naught but itself and takes naught but from itself.","Kahlil Gibran, The Prophet, 1923"],b:"Gibran was born in Lebanon. He taught that love is not a trade. You do not love to get something back. You love because love is good.",f:["“None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself.”","Bukhari 13"],a:"Do one loving thing today and expect nothing back."},
{s:"world",t:"The day the birds fly",img:"sakura",from:"Korea",b:"In Korea, the same story of the weaver girl and the cowherd is told on a day called Chilseok. People say the rain that falls that day is their happy tears when they finally meet. Every meeting after waiting is a small festival.",f:["“Verily, with hardship comes ease.”","Qur’an 94:6"],a:"Plan how you will celebrate your next meeting day."},
{s:"world",t:"Folding the long night",img:"moon",from:"Korea",b:"Hwang Jini, a famous Korean poet of the 1500s, wrote a tender wish: to cut a piece from the long winter night, fold it under a warm quilt, and unfold it on the night her love comes home.",f:["“Indeed, Allah is with the patient.”","Qur’an 2:153"],a:"Save something special to share only when he comes home."},
{s:"world",t:"If I knew it was a dream",img:"moon2",from:"Japan",q:["Had I known it was a dream, I would never have woken.","Ono no Komachi, Japan, 9th century"],b:"Ono no Komachi, Japan’s most loved woman poet, fell asleep thinking of the one she loved, and dreamed of him. Many hearts that live apart know this feeling.",f:["Before sleep, the Prophet ﷺ would say: “In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live.”","Bukhari 6324"],a:"Before sleep tonight, make dua for him and say goodnight."},
{s:"world",t:"The moon is beautiful",img:"moon",from:"Japan",b:"A famous Japanese story says a writer taught that a shy Japanese person might not say “I love you”. Instead they would say, “The moon is beautiful tonight, isn’t it?” Love can be gentle and hidden in soft words.",f:["“Modesty brings nothing but good.”","Bukhari 6117"],a:"Make a secret love code with him, like “The moon is beautiful.”"},
{s:"world",t:"Golden repairs",img:"tea2",from:"Japan",b:"In Japan, when a precious bowl breaks, some artists mend it with gold. This is called kintsugi. The cracks become the most beautiful part. A marriage can heal the same way: with patience, a hurt can become a golden line.",f:["“Reconciliation is best.”","Qur’an 4:128"],a:"Is there a small hurt between you? Mend it today with a kind word."},
/* SMILE */
{s:"smile",t:"No old women in Paradise?",b:"An old woman asked the Prophet ﷺ to pray she would enter Paradise. He said, “No old woman will enter Paradise.” She started to cry. He smiled and explained: Allah will make them young again!",f:["Shama’il al-Tirmidhi; Qur’an 56:35–37",""],a:"Tell this story to someone today and watch them smile."},
{s:"smile",t:"The baby camel",b:"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ for a camel to ride. He said, “I will give you a camel’s child.” The man said, “What will I do with a baby camel?” The Prophet ﷺ laughed: “Isn’t every camel the child of a camel?”",f:["Abu Dawud 4998",""],a:"Share one clean joke with him today."},
{s:"smile",t:"Guess who?",b:"The Prophet ﷺ once came up behind a Companion named Zahir in the market and hugged him, covering his eyes. Zahir said, “Who is this? Let me go!” When he realised, he leaned back happily into the hug.",f:["Shama’il al-Tirmidhi",""],a:"Surprise someone at home with a hug today."},
{s:"smile",t:"Juha and the donkey",b:"Juha and his son walked beside their donkey. People laughed: “Why not ride it?” So they both rode. Others shouted: “Poor donkey!” In the end they carried the donkey! You can’t please everyone.",f:["Seek Allah’s pleasure first, and people matter less.",""],a:"Do one thing today because it is right, not because people are watching."},
{s:"smile",t:"Looking under the light",b:"Juha was searching the street at night. “What did you lose?” “My ring.” “Where?” “In the house.” “Then why look here?” “Because there is more light here!”",f:["Look for answers where they really are.",""],a:"Laugh, then ask: am I looking for answers in the right place?"},
{s:"smile",t:"Eat, my coat, eat!",b:"Juha went to a feast in old clothes and nobody noticed him. He came back in a fine coat and was given the best seat. So he dipped his sleeve in the soup and said, “Eat, my coat, eat! They invited you, not me!”",f:["“Allah does not look at your faces or your wealth, but at your hearts.”","Muslim 2564"],a:"Treat someone today with honour, whatever they wear."},
{s:"smile",t:"The pot that died",b:"Juha borrowed a pot and returned it with a small pot inside. “Your pot had a baby!” The neighbour happily took it. Later Juha borrowed it again and didn’t return it. “Sorry, your pot died.” “Pots can’t die!” “But you believed it could have a baby!”",f:["",""],a:"Tell the children this story at bedtime."},
{s:"smile",t:"Five minutes",b:"When a husband says, “I’ll be ready in five minutes,” and a wife says, “I’m almost ready,” they both mean the same thing: about thirty minutes.",f:["",""],a:"Send him this joke. See if he agrees!"},
{s:"smile",t:"I think that’s what he said",b:"My husband says I never listen to him. At least, I think that’s what he said.",f:["",""],a:"Send this to him with a laughing face."},
{s:"smile",t:"When the Wi-Fi went off",b:"The Wi-Fi went off for an hour, so I talked to my family. They seem like nice people.",f:["",""],a:"Have one phone-free hour with the family today."},
{s:"smile",t:"Smiling is Sunnah",b:"The Prophet ﷺ smiled more than anyone his Companions knew. A smile is light on the face and charity in the scales.",f:["Tirmidhi 3641",""],a:"Smile at your reflection in the mirror. Yes, really!"},
{s:"smile",t:"Laugh, but not too much",b:"Laughter is healthy. But too much joking can make the heart careless. Balance is beautiful: laugh, then remember Allah.",f:["“Do not laugh too much, for too much laughter kills the heart.”","Tirmidhi 2305"],a:"Find one moment to laugh today, and one to remember Allah."},
{s:"smile",t:"Your clever phone",b:"Your phone knows all your secrets, your shopping, your late-night recipe searches… and still can’t remember where you put your keys.",f:["",""],a:"Name one funny thing that happened at home this week. Tell him."},/* ---- added 21 Nov 2026: more love from Asia and the Arab world. ALWAYS APPEND NEW CARDS AT THE END, with a fixed id. ---- */
{id:"w01",s:"world",img:"tea2",from:"China",t:"The tray raised to her eyebrows",b:"In old China, Meng Guang chose Liang Hong for his good character, not his money. Every day she served his meal holding the tray up to her eyebrows, as a sign of deep respect, and he honoured her the same way. Chinese people still use this picture for a happy couple: respect keeps love sweet.",f:["“The best of you are the best to their families.”","Tirmidhi 3895"],a:"Today, serve each other something, even a cup of tea on a call, with your full attention."},
{id:"w02",s:"world",img:"henna",from:"China",t:"He painted her eyebrows",b:"Zhang Chang was an important official in old China. Every morning he gently painted his wife’s eyebrows. People gossiped and the emperor asked him about it. He answered that between husband and wife there are sweeter things than painting eyebrows. Small daily care is real romance.",f:["Aisha (ra) used to comb the hair of the Prophet ﷺ.","Bukhari 296"],a:"On his next visit, do one small grooming kindness for each other."},
{id:"w03",s:"world",img:"moon2",from:"China",t:"Two fish in a small pond",b:"Chinese couples use an old picture of two fish in a drying pond, keeping each other wet so both can live. Today it praises partners who hold each other up through hard times, with whatever little they have.",f:["“Verily, with hardship comes ease.”","Qur’an 94:6"],a:"Remember one hard time you came through together. Thank him for staying by your side."},
{id:"w04",s:"world",img:"pinkroses",from:"China & Korea",t:"The mandarin ducks",b:"In China and Korea, mandarin ducks are a symbol of a faithful couple, because they are always seen in pairs. You will find them painted on wedding gifts and quilts. Two hearts, side by side, always.",f:["“Fulfil every promise. You will be asked about your promises.”","Qur’an 17:34"],a:"Send him the “Forever yours” postcard today."},
{id:"w05",s:"world",img:"moon",from:"China",t:"Being there is a love letter",b:"A popular Chinese saying goes: “Being there for someone is the longest love letter.” Big words fade. Showing up, day after day, says “I love you” the loudest. When you live apart, a call at the same time every day is a way of being there.",f:["“The most beloved deeds to Allah are the consistent ones, even if small.”","Bukhari 6464"],a:"Agree on one fixed time every day for a short call, just to hear each other."},
{id:"w06",s:"world",img:"sakura",from:"Japan",t:"Good Couples Day",b:"In Japan, 22 November is Good Couples Day. In Japanese, the date 11-22 sounds like “good couple”. Since 1988, couples use the day to thank each other, and many choose it as their wedding day.",f:["“Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah.”","Abu Dawud 4811"],a:"Make your own Good Couples Day: tell each other three things you appreciate."},
{id:"w07",s:"world",img:"peony",from:"Japan",t:"Kindness before asking",b:"The Japanese have a word, omoiyari. It means sensing what someone needs and quietly doing it before they ask. A warm drink when he is tired, silence when he needs rest, a smile when he is worried.",f:["“Allah helps His servant as long as the servant helps his brother.”","Muslim 2699"],a:"Do one thing he needs today without being asked."},
{id:"w08",s:"world",img:"tea",from:"Japan",t:"Love in a lunch box",b:"In Japan, many husbands and wives make each other beautiful lunch boxes, with food cut into hearts and smiling faces. It is love you can eat. Cooking for someone with care is a love letter too.",f:["“Even the bite of food you put in your wife’s mouth is rewarded.”","Bukhari 56"],a:"Cook something today thinking of him. Send him a photo of it."},
{id:"w09",s:"world",img:"tea2",from:"Japan",t:"Beautiful imperfection",b:"Wabi-sabi is a Japanese way of seeing beauty in things that are not perfect: an old bowl, a crooked branch, a faded cloth. Marriage is the same. You don’t love someone in spite of their imperfections. Slowly, you love them with them.",f:["“Let no believing man hate a believing woman. If he dislikes one of her traits, he will be pleased with another.”","Muslim 1469"],a:"Tell him one little imperfection of his that you have come to love."},
{id:"w10",s:"world",img:"moon2",from:"Japan",t:"The beauty of the pause",b:"Ma is the Japanese idea that a pause, a space or a silence has its own meaning. In marriage, a pause can save a conversation. When words get hot, a short silence lets the heart cool down.",f:["“If one of you becomes angry while standing, let him sit down.”","Abu Dawud 4782"],a:"Agree on a gentle “pause word” you both can use when a talk gets heated."},
{id:"w11",s:"world",img:"rings",from:"Korea",t:"The wooden geese",b:"At a traditional Korean wedding, the groom gives a pair of wooden geese, because wild geese stay with one partner for life. Couples keep the geese at home as a reminder of their promise.",f:["“And they have taken from you a solemn covenant.”","Qur’an 4:21"],a:"Choose a small object together to be “our symbol”, like the wooden geese."},
{id:"w12",s:"world",img:"hands2",from:"Korea",t:"Jeong: love that grows slowly",b:"Koreans talk about jeong, a deep, warm bond that grows slowly through shared moments, meals, troubles and laughter. It is not fireworks. It is roots. After years, it holds everything together.",f:["“And He placed between you affection and mercy.”","Qur’an 30:21"],a:"Write down three small daily habits you share that make you feel close."},
{id:"w13",s:"world",img:"arch",from:"Korea",t:"Counting days in hundreds",b:"Korean couples celebrate their 100th day together, then 200, then 1,000. Counting days makes every ordinary day feel part of a story. How many days have you two been married?",f:["“And speak of the blessings of your Lord.”","Qur’an 93:11"],a:"Work out how many days you have been married. Plan a small treat for the next 100."},
{id:"w14",s:"world",img:"peony",from:"Korea",t:"Reading the mood",b:"Koreans call it nunchi: the art of sensing how someone feels without being told. Notice his voice, his pauses, his short replies. Then ask softly, “How is your heart today?”",f:["“The believer is the mirror of his brother.”","Abu Dawud 4918"],a:"Ask him today: “How is your heart today, really?”"},
{id:"w15",s:"world",img:"tea",from:"Korea",t:"Matching things",b:"Korean couples love “couple items”: matching rings, mugs, phone cases or scarves. Every time you use yours, you remember the other one is using theirs. A halal, sweet idea for couples who live apart.",f:["“Give gifts to one another, and you will love one another.”","al-Adab al-Mufrad 594"],a:"Choose one matching item to get for both of you: a mug, prayer beads or a keyring."},
{id:"w16",s:"world",img:"paper",from:"India",t:"Two and a half letters",b:"Kabir, a weaver-poet of 15th-century India, wrote that people read book after book and never become wise. But whoever learns the two and a half letters of the word for love becomes truly wise. Love is the lesson books can’t finish.",f:["“The best of you are the best to their families.”","Tirmidhi 3895"],a:"Today, choose being kind over being right in one small moment."},
{id:"w17",s:"world",img:"arch",from:"India",t:"The abode of love",b:"In 1619, the Mughal emperor Jahangir built a garden in Kashmir for his wife Nur Jahan: Shalimar Bagh. Its name is often explained as “the abode of love”. They travelled there together again and again.",f:["Allah promises believing men and women “gardens beneath which rivers flow”.","Qur’an 9:72"],a:"Describe your dream garden to him. Plan a garden walk on his next visit."},
{id:"w18",s:"world",img:"taj",from:"India",t:"The empress on the coins",b:"Nur Jahan was the wife of the Mughal emperor Jahangir. He trusted her wisdom so much that coins were made with her name on them, the only Mughal empress honoured this way. A husband who trusts his wife’s mind, and a wife who uses it: that is a strong team.",f:["“And their affairs are decided by consultation among them.”","Qur’an 42:38"],a:"Ask his view on one decision, and share yours clearly."},
{id:"w19",s:"world",img:"tea2",from:"India",t:"Evening tea, long talks",b:"In many homes in India and Pakistan, evening tea is a daily pause. Work stops, cups are filled, and people simply talk. The tea is small; the talk is what matters.",f:["After his night prayer, the Prophet ﷺ would talk with Aisha if she was awake.","Bukhari 1161"],a:"Start a “tea call” ritual: same time, each with a cup, ten minutes of talk."},
{id:"w20",s:"world",img:"henna2",from:"India & Pakistan",t:"The name hidden in henna",b:"At many South Asian weddings, the groom’s name or initials are hidden somewhere in the bride’s henna. Later he has to search for it, while everyone laughs and waits. A playful game of love.",f:["The Prophet ﷺ encouraged women to colour their hands with henna.","Abu Dawud 4166"],a:"Hide his initial in a drawing or your henna, send a photo, and see if he can find it."},
{id:"w21",s:"world",img:"tea",from:"Turkey",t:"One coffee, forty years",b:"A famous Turkish saying goes: a cup of coffee is remembered for forty years. One shared moment of kindness can be remembered for a lifetime. In marriage, the small moments are the big ones.",f:["“Do not think little of any good deed, even meeting your brother with a cheerful face.”","Muslim 2626"],a:"Have a coffee or tea date on video call, each with your own cup."},
{id:"w22",s:"world",img:"tea2",from:"Turkey",t:"The salty coffee test",b:"When a Turkish family comes to ask for a bride, the bride serves coffee to everyone. But in the groom’s cup she puts salt instead of sugar! If he drinks it with a smile, he has shown his patience and good heart.",f:["Allah loves “those who restrain anger and pardon people”.","Qur’an 3:134"],a:"Ask him playfully: “Would you have drunk my salty coffee?” Enjoy the answer."},
{id:"w23",s:"world",img:"tea",from:"Turkey",t:"The heart wants a talk",b:"Another Turkish saying: the heart wants neither coffee nor a coffee house. The heart wants a good talk, and coffee is only the excuse. What we really long for is to be heard.",f:["“A good word is charity.”","Bukhari 2989"],a:"Tonight, ask him one deep question, then just listen."},
{id:"w24",s:"world",img:"tulips",from:"Turkey",t:"The tulip’s secret",b:"Tulips were loved in the Ottoman world. People noticed that in Arabic letters, the word for tulip, lale, uses the same letters as the name of Allah. So the flower became a quiet reminder: the best love leads back to Him.",f:["“Verily, in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find rest.”","Qur’an 13:28"],a:"Send him a flower photo with a short dua for him."},
{id:"w25",s:"world",img:"bouquet",from:"Arabia",t:"Fifty words for love",b:"Imam Ibn al-Qayyim listed about fifty Arabic words for love, each a different shade. Hubb is love. Wudd is warm, gentle love, close to Allah’s name al-Wadud. Shawq is longing. Hanin is tender yearning. Ulfa is easy closeness.",f:["“And He is the Forgiving, the Loving (al-Wadud).”","Qur’an 85:14"],a:"Use one of these Arabic love words with him today. Tell him what it means."},
{id:"w26",s:"world",img:"rose2",from:"Arabia",t:"Sweet Arabic names",b:"Arabic is rich in sweet names. Ya habibi: my beloved. Ya ‘umri: my life. Ya rouhi: my soul. Ya albi: my heart. And qurrat ‘ayni: the comfort of my eyes, the same words the Qur’an uses for a loving family.",f:["“Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and children comfort to our eyes.”","Qur’an 25:74"],a:"Choose your favourite Arabic sweet name and use it in your next message."},
{id:"w27",s:"world",img:"hands",from:"Arabia",t:"He knew her moods",b:"The Prophet ﷺ told Aisha: “I know when you are pleased with me and when you are upset.” When pleased she would swear “by the Lord of Muhammad”, and when upset “by the Lord of Ibrahim”. She smiled: “Yes, but I only leave out your name.”",f:["The Prophet ﷺ noticed even the small signs of his wife’s feelings.","Bukhari 5228"],a:"Tell him one small sign that shows him you are happy."},
{id:"w28",s:"world",img:"moon",from:"Arabia",t:"Antara and Abla",b:"Antara was born a slave in old Arabia, but his love for Abla pushed him to become a great knight and one of the most famous Arab poets. Even far away, his poems remembered her. Real love makes us want to grow.",f:["“Allah does not change a people until they change what is in themselves.”","Qur’an 13:11"],a:"Tell him how his love makes you want to grow."},
{id:"w29",s:"world",img:"tea2",from:"Arabia",t:"The welcome of honour",b:"Across the Arab world, a guest is welcomed with Arabic coffee, dates and warm words before anything else. Imagine giving that same honour to your husband when he comes home after a long journey.",f:["“Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honour his guest.”","Bukhari 6019"],a:"Plan exactly how you will welcome him at his next homecoming."},
{id:"h01",s:"his",img:"hands",t:"Respect is how he feels loved",b:"Researcher Shaunti Feldhahn asked hundreds of men a hard question: would you rather feel unloved, or feel disrespected? Three out of four chose unloved. For many men, respect and love are the same thing. When you respect him, he feels loved. When you belittle him, he feels unloved, even if you love him deeply.",f:["“Live with them in kindness.”","Qur’an 4:19"],a:"Tell him one specific thing you respect about him. Say why."},
{id:"h02",s:"his",img:"paper",t:"Say what you admire",b:"Marriage counsellor Willard Harley spent years asking husbands what they need most. One answer kept coming back: an admiring wife. A man works hard, often without thanks. A few words of honest admiration from you can carry him through a whole hard week.",f:["Khadijah (ra) told the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah will never disgrace you. You keep family ties, you help the weak, you honour guests.”","Bukhari 3"],a:"Write down three qualities you admire in him. Send them today."},
{id:"h03",s:"his",img:"moon2",from:"Khadijah",t:"Khadijah’s comfort",b:"When the first revelation came, the Prophet ﷺ came home shaking: “Cover me, cover me.” Khadijah did not ask many questions. She covered him, calmed him, reminded him of his good character, and then took him to someone who could help. Comfort first, then solutions.",f:["Bukhari 3",""],a:"Next time he is stressed, ask first: “How can I help you?” Then listen."},
{id:"h04",s:"his",img:"tea",from:"Umm Salamah",t:"The wife whose advice saved the day",b:"At Hudaybiyah, the companions were upset and did not move when the Prophet ﷺ told them to. He went to his wife Umm Salamah, troubled. She said: go out, speak to no one, and do it yourself. He did, and everyone followed. A wise wife is a husband’s best adviser, especially in private.",f:["Bukhari 2731",""],a:"Share one good idea with him privately and gently, as a friend."},
{id:"h05",s:"his",img:"henna2",from:"Arabia",t:"A mother’s ten pieces of advice",b:"Long ago, an Arab mother named Umamah gave her daughter ten pieces of advice on her wedding day. Some of them: be content with him. Care about what his eyes see and what his nose smells. Watch his meal times and sleep. Keep his secrets. Don’t be cheerful when he is sad, or gloomy when he is happy. Her daughter’s marriage became famous for its peace.",f:["“The best of women is the one who pleases him when he looks at her.”","Nasa’i 3231"],a:"Choose one of these ten and practise it this week."},
{id:"h06",s:"his",img:"arch",t:"Sakinah: be his place of rest",b:"This app is named after a word in the Qur’an. Allah made spouses so that we find sakinah, calm and rest, in each other. A man comes from a world of pressure. When your voice is the calm part of his day, home becomes the place he runs to, not runs from.",f:["“He created for you spouses so that you may find rest in them.”","Qur’an 30:21"],a:"On your next call, start with a smile and one piece of good news."},
{id:"h07",s:"his",img:"moon",t:"When he goes quiet",b:"Many men go quiet when they are under pressure. They think alone, solve the problem in their head, and then come back. It is easy to think, “He doesn’t care” or “I did something wrong.” Usually, neither is true. Give him a little space, and a warm door to walk back through.",f:["“Allah is with the patient.”","Qur’an 2:153"],a:"When he is quiet, send: “I’m here when you’re ready. No rush.”"},
{id:"h08",s:"his",img:"crate",t:"Let him be your hero",b:"Most men love to provide, protect and fix things. It is how many of them say “I love you.” When you thank him for what he provides, and let him help you, he feels useful and proud. When his effort goes unnoticed, he slowly stops trying.",f:["“The coin you spend on your family has the greatest reward.”","Muslim 995"],a:"Thank him today for one thing he provides. Name it clearly."},
{id:"h09",s:"his",img:"bokeh",t:"Be his playmate too",b:"Harley found that many husbands want their wife as a fun companion, someone to enjoy things with, not only to solve problems with. The Prophet ﷺ raced Aisha twice. She won the first time. Later he won and laughed: “This one is for that one.”",f:["Abu Dawud 2578",""],a:"Do something fun together on a call: a quiz, a game, or the same video."},
{id:"h10",s:"his",img:"rose2",t:"Look your best for him",b:"Umamah’s old advice said: care about what his eyes see. This is not about being perfect. It is about care. Men notice effort. A nice dress, a little kohl, a smile, especially on a video call, tells him: “I still want to look beautiful for you.” And Islam asks husbands to do the same for wives.",f:["Ibn Abbas: “I love to dress up for my wife, as I love her to dress up for me.”","Tafsir of Qur’an 2:228"],a:"Dress up for your next video call. Don’t say why. Just smile."},
{id:"h11",s:"his",img:"redrose",t:"He wants to feel wanted",b:"Men don’t only want to be needed for money or fixing things. Deep down, they want to be wanted, desired and missed. When you tell him you miss him, not just his help, his heart grows warm. In Islam, loving closeness between husband and wife is even rewarded.",f:["“In the intimacy of one of you there is charity.”","Muslim 1006"],a:"Send him: “I miss you. Not your help. You.”"},
{id:"h12",s:"his",img:"hands2",t:"Praise in public, correct in private",b:"Feldhahn found that men feel deep pain when they are corrected or mocked in front of others. A gentle word in private works better than a sharp word in public. And praise in front of his family or friends stays in his heart for years.",f:["“Whoever covers the faults of a Muslim, Allah will cover his faults on the Day of Resurrection.”","Bukhari 2442"],a:"Praise him in front of someone this week."},
{id:"h13",s:"his",img:"tea2",t:"No “I told you so”",b:"Share your view clearly. That is your right. But after you decide together, stand behind the decision. If it goes wrong, don’t say “I told you so.” Say “We will fix it together.” This builds a trust that makes him listen to you even more next time.",f:["“And consult them in the matter.”","Qur’an 3:159"],a:"This week, replace “I told you so” with “We’ll fix it together.”"},
{id:"h14",s:"his",img:"henna",from:"Asma bint Abi Bakr",t:"Asma and the date stones",b:"When Asma married Zubair, he owned only a horse. She fed the horse and carried date stones on her head from far away. One day the Prophet ﷺ offered her a ride. She felt shy and walked. Zubair later told her: “Seeing you carry those stones was harder on me than anything.” Struggles shared with love become proud memories.",f:["Bukhari 5224",""],a:"Tell him one hard time you are proud you both came through."},
{id:"h15",s:"his",img:"tea",t:"His small bids",b:"Marriage researcher John Gottman studied newlyweds for six years. Couples who stayed together had turned toward each other’s small “bids” for attention 86% of the time. Couples who divorced: only 33%. Men make bids too: a joke, a football score, a photo. Answering them warmly matters more than you think.",f:["“Your smile for your brother is charity.”","Tirmidhi 1956"],a:"When he shares something small today, ask one curious question about it."},
{id:"h16",s:"his",img:"bouquet",t:"Remember the good",b:"The Prophet ﷺ warned against forgetting years of kindness because of one bad day, saying, “I never saw any good from you.” In hard moments, the mind remembers only the hurt. Make a habit of remembering his good deeds, so one bad day never erases them.",f:["Bukhari 29",""],a:"Write five good things he did for you this year. Read them on a hard day."},
{id:"h17",s:"his",img:"peony",from:"Nigeria",t:"Patience is the medicine",b:"Hausa wisdom says: Hakuri maganin duniya, patience is the medicine of the world. Another proverb says: Zaman lafiya ya fi zama dan sarki, living in peace is better than being a king’s child. A peaceful home is a treasure that money cannot buy.",f:["“O you who believe, be patient and outdo each other in patience.”","Qur’an 3:200"],a:"Next time you disagree, wait one hour before you reply."},
{id:"h18",s:"his",img:"arch",t:"Make home his favourite place",b:"A man away from home carries a picture of it in his heart: the smell of the food, the sound of the children, the welcome at the door. Even from far away, you can make that picture warm. When he comes back, let home feel like the best place on earth.",f:["“Allah has made your homes a place of rest for you.”","Qur’an 16:80"],a:"Plan his homecoming meal now. Ask him to guess what it is."},
{id:"m01",s:"hers",img:"hands",t:"The measure of a man",b:"The Prophet ﷺ gave men a simple test. Not wealth, not titles, not how people see you at work. The test is how you treat your family at home. He said he was the best of people to his own family. A good husband is a great man.",f:["“The best of you are the best to their families, and I am the best of you to my family.”","Tirmidhi 3895"],a:"Ask her: “What would make your week easier?” Then do it."},
{id:"m02",s:"hers",img:"tea2",t:"He served his family",b:"Aisha was asked what the Prophet ﷺ did at home. She said he was busy serving his family, and when prayer came he went to pray. He mended his own clothes and fixed his own sandals. Helping at home is not small. It is Sunnah.",f:["Bukhari 676",""],a:"On your next visit, take one chore fully off her hands."},
{id:"m03",s:"hers",img:"bokeh",t:"Race her, laugh with her",b:"On a journey, the Prophet ﷺ told the people to go ahead. Then he raced Aisha, and she won. Years later they raced again. He won, and smiled: “This one is for that one.” The best man who ever lived made time to play with his wife.",f:["Abu Dawud 2578",""],a:"Play a game with her on your next call. Let the laughter win."},
{id:"m04",s:"hers",img:"tea",t:"The same spot on the cup",b:"Aisha said: I would drink, then pass the cup to the Prophet ﷺ, and he would put his mouth where mine had been. I would bite a piece of meat, and he would eat from the same place. Small, playful closeness says: I love everything about you.",f:["Muslim 300",""],a:"On your next visit, share a cup of tea this way. Watch her smile."},
{id:"m05",s:"hers",img:"moon2",t:"He listened to the long story",b:"Aisha once told the Prophet ﷺ a long story about eleven women describing their husbands. He listened to the end. Then he said: “I am to you as Abu Zar’ was to Umm Zar’,” the best husband in the story. Listening fully is a gift.",f:["Bukhari 5189",""],a:"Let her talk for ten minutes today. No advice, no phone. Just listen."},
{id:"m06",s:"hers",img:"tea2",t:"Accept her influence",b:"John Gottman followed newlyweds for years. Husbands who accepted their wives’ influence, who listened and let her ideas change their decisions, had happier and more stable marriages. When a husband refuses to share power, Gottman found an 81% chance the marriage will fall apart.",f:["The Prophet ﷺ took Umm Salamah’s advice at Hudaybiyah, and it worked.","Bukhari 2731"],a:"This week, follow one suggestion she makes, and tell her you did."},
{id:"m07",s:"hers",img:"rings",t:"Dress up for her",b:"Ibn Abbas, the great scholar of the Qur’an, said: “I love to dress up for my wife, just as I love her to dress up for me.” He read it in the verse that wives have rights like the rights over them. Looking good for her is part of your duty, and your love.",f:["“And they have rights similar to those over them, in kindness.”","Qur’an 2:228"],a:"Wear your best and some perfume for your next video call."},
{id:"m08",s:"hers",img:"redrose",t:"Say her name with pride",b:"Someone asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Who is the most beloved person to you?” He did not hide it. He said: “Aisha.” About Khadijah he said: “I was given her love.” Real men are not shy to say whom they love.",f:["Bukhari 3662 · Muslim 2435",""],a:"Tell her clearly: “You are the most beloved person to me.”"},
{id:"m09",s:"hers",img:"bouquet",t:"Love the people she loves",b:"Years after Khadijah died, the Prophet ﷺ still sent gifts of meat to her friends. Loving a woman includes honouring her mother, her sisters and her friends. When you are kind to her people, she feels it as kindness to her.",f:["Bukhari 3818",""],a:"Call or greet her mother or sister this week, just to be kind."},
{id:"m10",s:"hers",img:"henna",t:"Calm when she is upset",b:"Once, one of the Prophet’s wives sent food while he was in Aisha’s house. In a moment of jealousy, Aisha knocked the dish and it broke. He did not shout. He quietly gathered the pieces and the food and said gently, “Your mother became jealous.” Then he replaced the dish.",f:["Bukhari 5225",""],a:"When she is upset, lower your voice and soften your words."},
{id:"m11",s:"hers",img:"pinkroses",t:"Gently with the glass",b:"On a journey, a man named Anjashah drove the camels fast while the women rode. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Gently, Anjashah! Gently with the glass vessels.” He compared women’s hearts to fine glass: precious, beautiful, and worth handling with care.",f:["Bukhari 6149",""],a:"Notice one harsh habit in your speech, and soften it this week."},
{id:"m12",s:"hers",img:"crate",t:"Spending on her is worship",b:"The Prophet ﷺ said the best coin you spend is the one you spend on your family. Even the food you put in your wife’s mouth is charity. Providing for her is not only a duty. With the right intention, every bill you pay is written as good deeds.",f:["Muslim 995",""],a:"Send her a small surprise gift this week, with a sweet note."},
{id:"m13",s:"hers",img:"tea",t:"Listen, don’t fix",b:"Linguist Deborah Tannen found that many women talk to feel close, while many men talk to solve problems. So when she shares a worry, a man jumps to advice, and she feels unheard. Often she doesn’t want a solution. She wants you with her.",f:["“A good word is charity.”","Bukhari 2989"],a:"Ask her: “Do you want ideas, or do you want me to listen?”"},
{id:"m14",s:"hers",img:"paper",t:"Answer her bids",b:"Gottman found that couples who stay married turn toward each other’s small bids 86% of the time. Couples who divorce: 33%. A postcard, a heartbeat, a photo of the children, a “guess what?” These are bids. Each warm reply is a deposit in her heart.",f:["“Do not belittle any good deed.”","Muslim 2626"],a:"Today, reply warmly to every message she sends. No “ok” or “k”."},
{id:"m15",s:"hers",img:"moon",t:"He waited until she was tired",b:"Some Abyssinians were playing with spears in the mosque. Aisha wanted to watch. The Prophet ﷺ stood and shielded her so she could see, and he waited and waited until she herself was tired and left. He never said, “Hurry up.”",f:["Bukhari 5190",""],a:"Watch something she enjoys with her, until she is the one who stops."},
{id:"m16",s:"hers",img:"hands2",t:"Her many roles",b:"While you are away, she carries the home: the children, the cooking, the visitors, the worries. Harley found wives need affection, real conversation, honesty, support, and a husband committed to family. Your thanks and attention are the fuel that keeps her going.",f:["“Live with them in kindness.”","Qur’an 4:19"],a:"Thank her for three specific things she did for the children this week."},
{id:"m17",s:"hers",img:"rose1",t:"His knee for her step",b:"When Safiyyah wanted to climb onto her camel, the Prophet ﷺ sat down and put his knee forward so she could step on it and climb up. A leader of nations, bending his knee for his wife. Small gentleman acts are Sunnah too.",f:["Bukhari 4211",""],a:"On your next visit, do one gentleman act: open the door, carry the bags."},
{id:"m18",s:"hers",img:"sakura",t:"Call her by a sweet name",b:"The Prophet ﷺ had playful names for Aisha. Once he said: “Ya Aish, this is Jibril sending you salam.” He shortened her name with love. A special name, used only by you, tells her she is special only to you.",f:["Bukhari 3768",""],a:"Choose a sweet nickname for her today. Use it in your next message."},
{id:"j01",s:"smile",img:"bokeh",from:"Sunnah",t:"The camel’s baby",b:"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ for a camel to ride. He said: “I will give you the baby of a camel.” The man was confused: “What will I do with a baby camel?” The Prophet ﷺ smiled: “Does any camel give birth to anything except camels?” Every camel is some camel’s baby!",f:["He ﷺ said: “I joke, but I only say what is true.”","Tirmidhi · Shama’il 236–237"],a:"Tell him a joke today that is funny and true."},
{id:"j02",s:"smile",img:"tulips",from:"Sunnah",t:"No old women in Paradise",b:"An old woman asked the Prophet ﷺ to pray that she enters Paradise. He said: “Old women don’t enter Paradise.” She walked away crying. He called her back, smiling: “They won’t enter as old women. Allah will make them young again.” She was delighted.",f:["Shama’il at-Tirmidhi 239",""],a:"Make someone laugh today, gently, without hurting anyone."},
{id:"j03",s:"smile",img:"peony",from:"Sunnah",t:"Who will buy this servant?",b:"Zahir was a simple desert man, not handsome. One day the Prophet ﷺ came up behind him in the market, hugged him, and called out: “Who will buy this servant?” Zahir laughed: “You will find me cheap, O Messenger of Allah!” He replied: “But to Allah, you are not cheap.”",f:["Shama’il at-Tirmidhi 238",""],a:"Surprise him with a playful hug on his next visit."},
{id:"j04",s:"smile",img:"ranun",from:"Sunnah",t:"The little bird",b:"Anas had a little brother, Abu Umair, who had a pet bird. When the bird died, the boy was sad. The Prophet ﷺ would greet him with a rhyme: “Ya Aba Umair, ma fa’al an-nughair?” Oh Abu Umair, what happened to the little bird? He also teased Anas: “Oh you with two ears!”",f:["Bukhari 6129",""],a:"Make up a funny rhyme for the children or for him."},
{id:"j05",s:"smile",img:"tea2",from:"Turkey",t:"You are right too",b:"Nasreddin Hodja was a judge. The first man told his story. Hodja said: “You are right.” The second man told the opposite story. Hodja said: “You are right.” His wife was listening: “Husband, they can’t both be right!” Hodja thought, then said: “Wife, you are right too.”",f:["Nasreddin Hodja, 13th-century Turkey",""],a:"Next small argument, say: “You are right too,” and see who laughs first."},
{id:"j06",s:"smile",img:"moon",from:"Turkey",t:"The shot coat",b:"One night Hodja saw a white figure in his garden. A thief! He shot an arrow. In the morning he found it was his own coat, washed by his wife and hung to dry. He fell to his knees: “Thank God! Thank God!” His wife asked why. “If I had been inside that coat, I would be dead!”",f:["Nasreddin Hodja",""],a:"Find one thing to thank Allah for in today’s small trouble."},
{id:"j07",s:"smile",img:"tulips",from:"Turkey",t:"The pot that had a baby",b:"Hodja borrowed a big pot from his neighbour. He returned it with a small pot inside: “Your pot gave birth!” The neighbour happily took both. Later Hodja borrowed it again and didn’t return it. “Sorry, your pot died.” “Pots can’t die!” “You believed it could give birth.”",f:["Nasreddin Hodja",""],a:"Tell this story to the children tonight."},
{id:"j08",s:"smile",img:"tea",from:"Turkey",t:"Eat, my coat, eat!",b:"Hodja went to a wedding in his old clothes. Nobody greeted him. He went home, put on his best coat, and came back. Now everyone welcomed him and gave him the best food. Hodja dipped his sleeve in the soup: “Eat, my coat, eat! You are the one they invited.”",f:["“Allah does not look at your appearance or wealth, but at your hearts and deeds.”","Muslim 2564"],a:"Today, be extra kind to someone others ignore."},
{id:"j09",s:"smile",img:"bokeh",from:"Arabia",t:"Juha’s lost donkey",b:"Juha lost his donkey. He searched everywhere, saying, “Alhamdulillah! Alhamdulillah!” People were puzzled: “Why are you praising God? Your donkey is lost!” Juha said: “Thank God I wasn’t riding it. I would be lost too!”",f:["Juha, Arab folk tales",""],a:"Share one funny “at least…” about your day with him."},
{id:"j10",s:"smile",img:"ranun",from:"Arabia",t:"Juha, his son and the donkey",b:"Juha and his son both rode the donkey. People said: “Poor donkey!” So the son rode alone. “Rude boy, letting his father walk!” So Juha rode alone. “Cruel father!” So both walked. “Fools! They have a donkey and walk!” Juha laughed: “You can never please everyone.”",f:["Juha, Arab folk tales",""],a:"Stop worrying about one person’s opinion today. Please Allah first."},
{id:"j11",s:"smile",img:"paper",from:"India",t:"How many bangles?",b:"Emperor Akbar asked Birbal: “How many bangles does your wife wear?” Birbal didn’t know. Akbar laughed. Birbal asked: “How many steps lead up to your palace, Your Majesty?” Akbar didn’t know, though he climbed them every day. “Exactly,” smiled Birbal. “We miss what we see every day.”",f:["Akbar and Birbal, Indian folk tales",""],a:"Notice one detail about him you’ve never asked. Ask today."},
{id:"j12",s:"smile",img:"tea2",from:"India",t:"Who ate the mangoes?",b:"Akbar and Birbal were eating mangoes. As a joke, Akbar quietly pushed all his mango seeds in front of Birbal. “Birbal! Look how many mangoes you ate!” Birbal looked at the empty space in front of Akbar: “At least I left the seeds, Your Majesty. You ate yours too!”",f:["Akbar and Birbal",""],a:"Play a little trick on him on your next video call."},
{id:"j13",s:"smile",img:"moon2",from:"Turkey",t:"Looking where the light is",b:"Hodja was searching for something under a street lamp. A friend asked: “What did you lose?” “My ring.” “Where did you drop it?” “Inside my house.” “Then why search here?” “Because there is more light here!” We often look for happiness in the wrong places.",f:["Nasreddin Hodja",""],a:"Ask each other: where are we looking for happiness in the wrong place?"}];
